          {
            "id": "About-home",
            "type": "About",
            "band": "plain",
            "bleed": "full",
            "variant": "letter",
            "copy": {
              "kicker": "Who we are",
              "heading": "This ain’t your grandma’s nonprofit",
              "role": "But she’s welcome, too.",
              "body": "Unlabeled is for Texans tired of being told who they are before anyone hears them. From the outlaws to the rule followers, everybody’s got a place here.\n\nWe listen past the labels, ask hard questions, and make room for honest conversations about the things people actually live with: schools, property taxes, jobs, roads, health care, and the future we’re handing our kids.\n\nWe’re not here to tell you what to think or who to vote for. We’re here to put people and policy ahead of party talking points. Texas works better when neighbors can talk honestly, disagree respectfully, and still move forward.\n\nThis is powered by people willing to give a damn. Follow us, show up, share your perspective, and help build a Texas conversation that puts listening first.",
              "signature": "Leave the labels to the rest of the country. Just bring yourself."
            },
            "media": {},
